Verify
  • Press Win + R, type dhcpmgmt.msc, and press Enter to open the DHCP console.
• In the left pane, expand your server name, expand IPv4, and click on your active Scope.
• Click on Address Leases in the left column.
• Look at the middle pane:• If you see client devices listed with their IP addresses and hostnames, your DHCP server is actively handing out configurations.
• If the list is empty, no client has requested an IP address yet, or devices on your network are still using a different router's DHCP.
  
